senses
  entry
    definition "a detailed list of all the items in stock"
    id oewn-06504655-n
    partOfSpeech n
    synonyms ("stock list")
  entry
    definition "the merchandise that a shop has on hand"
    examples ("they carried a vast inventory of hardware" "they stopped selling in exact sizes in order to reduce inventory")
    id oewn-04328672-n
    partOfSpeech n
    synonyms (stock)
  entry
    definition "(accounting) the value of a firm's current assets including raw materials and work in progress and finished goods"
    id oewn-13433706-n
    partOfSpeech n
  entry
    definition "a collection of resources"
    examples ("he dipped into his intellectual armory to find an answer")
    id oewn-05641904-n
    partOfSpeech n
    synonyms (armory armoury)
  entry
    definition "making an itemized list of merchandise or supplies on hand"
    examples ("an inventory may be necessary to see if anything is missing" "they held an inventory every month")
    id oewn-01013367-n
    partOfSpeech n
    synonyms (inventorying stocktaking stock-taking)
  entry
    definition "make or include in an itemized record or report"
    examples ("Inventory all books before the end of the year")
    id oewn-02477918-v
    partOfSpeech v
    synonyms ("take stock" stock-take)
